  "title": "Until vs By – Grammar Shorts",
  "description": "Until и by отвечают на разные вопросы о времени: продолжалось до момента или должно завершиться не позже deadline.",
  "theory": {
    "rule_id": "RULE-Grammar Shorts-26-RU",
    "lesson_num": 26,
    "title": "Правила: Until vs By – Grammar Shorts",
    "level": "SHORTS",
    "overview": "Until и by отвечают на разные вопросы о времени: продолжалось до момента или должно завершиться не позже deadline.",
    "main_rule": "Until = situation/action continues up to a time. By = deadline/latest time something will happen.",
    "form": "verb + until + time. verb + by + time.",
    "when_why": "Для continuous duration → until. Для deadline/completion → by.",
    "examples": "I'll work until six. → Я буду работать до шести.\nShe stayed there until Friday. → Она оставалась там до пятницы.\nPlease finish it by six. → Закончи это к шести.\nI'll have sent the report by Friday. → Я отправлю отчёт к пятнице.",
    "special_cases": "Until can mean «не раньше», depending on context: Send it until Friday is not a normal way to express a deadline.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ Please finish it until six. → ✅ Please finish it by six.\n✅ I won't send it until Friday. → Здесь until means «не раньше пятницы».",
    "dont_confuse": "until = continuation up to a time.\nby = deadline/latest time.",
    "quick_summary": "until → continues to.\nby → completed no later than."
  },
